<title>DENMARK: Denmark's sells unit to Unilever.</title>
<headline>Denmark's sells unit to Unilever.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish cleaning and service group ISS said on Monday that it had agreed to sell its ISS Darenas International trading company to Unilever's DiverseyLever unit.</p>
<p>An ISS statement gave no price for the sale but said that ISS Darenas had 1996 turnover of 170 million crowns.</p>
<p>It said that the sale was part of a strategy of concentrating on the core business of industrial cleaning, catering and other services.</p>
<p>It added that the drop in operating profits caused by the divestment would be recovered with the purchase of new, unspecified, businesses in the coming months. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
